-- Eliminates the O(N²) single-Word bignum growth of un-renormalized rANS in lib/compress.cub
-- by keeping the active rANS state strictly bounded in [L, 256·L) and flushing/refilling
-- base-256 bytes on a LIFO byte stream at O(1) arithmetic cost per symbol:
--   1. sr-flush / sr-refill: exact single-byte base-256 bijection via wdiv-mod.
--   2. sr-flush-loop / sr-refill-loop: multi-byte renormalization with universal inductive
--      roundtrip theorem (sr-renorm-ok) for any bounded state s ∈ [L, 256·L).
--   3. sr-enc-step / sr-dec-step: single-symbol streaming rANS step with exact bijection
--      theorem (sr-step-ok) composing rans-step-ok (lib/compress.cub) with sr-renorm-ok.
--   4. sr-enc-list / sr-dec-list: full streaming list codec with concrete kernel-checked (refl)
--      bounded-state witnesses proving exact roundtrip and steady-state s ∈ [L, 256·L).

